{
  "comment": "The applications both sides build. One entry per application, and one scene per shot: a real application is a window and the dialogs it opens, so its dialogs are scenes of it rather than applications of their own. A scene's mode is content (the application builds a widget for the window's content area), window (it builds its own toplevel, because a GtkWindow cannot be another window's content) or overlay (it presents a dialog or popover over the window, because those live above the content area rather than in it). Both renderers read this, so neither has a list of its own.",
